app orb-disk-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "Design contract for `orb disk` (full parity with tools/almadar-disk, which it replaces): report what fills the disk on a machine working the monorepo, and clear it. REPORT: the first line is the volume (`Disk: <used> used, <free> free of <total> (<pct>%)`), a blank line, then one row per registry item, largest first (sizeless items last), each `<size padded to 7>  <tag padded to 6>  <id padded to 28>  <label>` with tag keep (not clearable), safe (in the batch), danger or cost; then a blank line, `safe batch: ~<size>  →  orb disk --safe --yes` and `one item:   orb disk --clear <id> [--yes]` (the arrow line names the program through the command knob; status 200, exit 0). Sizes print as B, K, M, G or T with one decimal below 10, none from 10; a sizeless item prints a dash. `--json` answers one document tagged kind report: { kind, df: { totalBytes, usedBytes, freeBytes, usePct }, items: [{ id, label, category, note?, batch, clearable, danger, sizeless, bytes (null when sizeless) }], scannedAt (ISO UTC) }. ITEMS: the 30 darwin items of the TS registry in its order; fixed home or working-directory paths are sized by one `du -sk`, and the walk items from `find`: node_modules (every node_modules under the working directory, not descending into one), rust-target-debug and rust-target-release (target/debug and target/release beside every Cargo.toml, so a target/ that is a symlink is measured through the link, where the TS tool, whose find only sees real directories, reports 0), turbo-cache (.turbo) and python-venvs (.venv) (never inside node_modules or .git), verify-temp-apps (/private/tmp/orbital-verify-*), claude-stale-sessions (under /private/tmp/claude-<uid>: a session directory with nothing modified in the last 48 hours whole, and in a live session each scratchpad or tasks entry with nothing modified in the last 48 hours); each walk group is sized by its own `du -sk`. CLEAR: `--safe` selects the clearable items whose batch flag is set, `--clear <id>` the one clearable item with that id (`--safe` wins when both are given; the token after `--clear` is always the id, even when it is `--yes`); an id that is unknown or not clearable answers `unknown or non-clearable item: <id>` and `clearable: <ids>` (or { kind: error, error, clearable } with `--json`), status 500, before any probe runs. Without `--yes` nothing is changed: the answer lists `<size padded to 7>  <id>  — <note>` per target (and, for the rm items, the existing paths under it, indented 11 spaces) then `dry run: ~<size> would be cleared. Add --yes to clear.` (or { kind: preview, bytes, targets: [{ id, bytes, paths }] }), status 200. With `--yes` each target is cleared in order and a failure of one does not stop the next. The actions: rm items run `rm -rf --` on the existing paths that pass the safety rule, and log `disk: refusing to remove unsafe paths: <paths>` for those that do not; contents items (chrome-disk-cache, cargo-registry-cache, xcode-derived-data, sccache, core-simulator-caches, trash) keep the directory and run `find <dir> -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -exec rm -rf -- {} +` when it passes the rule; cmd items run `pnpm store prune`, `brew cleanup --prune=all` or `xcrun simctl delete unavailable` and never fail; node-modules runs `find <cwd> -type d -name node_modules -prune -exec rm -rf -- {} +` and never fails. THE SAFETY RULE: a path is removed only when it is strictly below HOME at least two levels deep (never HOME itself nor a direct child) or inside /tmp or /private/tmp, and it holds no `/./` or `/../` segment. The log lines are `disk: clearing <id>`, `disk: rm -rf <path>` and `disk: clear <id> failed: <error>`; the answer is the listing, the log, a blank line and `freed <size>; now <size> free` (freed = max 0 of used before minus used after a second df), then one `failed: <id>: <error>` line per failure, status 500 and exit 1 when any target failed; `--json` answers { kind: cleared, cleared, failed: [{ id, error }], freedBytes, df, log } instead. Any other argument answers `usage: orb disk [--json] [--safe | --clear <id>] [--yes]` (status 400, exit 2); a probe that cannot run answers `<code>: <message>` (status 500, exit 1). DIVERGENCES FROM THE TS TOOL: unknown arguments answer the usage where the TS tool ignores them; the working directory is the repo root (no walk-up to the directory holding orbital-rust and packages); a clear dry run measures every item before listing the targets; the rm items run one `rm -rf` over all their safe paths and report its stderr as the error; the footer names `orb disk` where the TS tool names `pnpm disk`."
]

type DiskItem = { id : string!, label : string!, tag : string!, bytes : number! }
type DiskReport = { totalBytes : number!, usedBytes : number!, freeBytes : number!, usePct : number!, items : [DiskItem]! }

orbital OrbDiskSpec {
  expects trait OrbDisk {
    state ready
    state parsing
    state measuring
    state clearing
    emits {
      DISK_ANSWERED { status : number!  body : string! }
    }
  }
  expects page "/orb-disk" -> OrbDisk
}
